+# smallpt browser lab
+
+Kevin Beason's smallpt C++ path tracer compiled to WebAssembly, with progressive rendering in a Web Worker. Open `index.html` through your static hosting environment. The compiled assets are checked in; no build is required to use the page. The worker and WebAssembly need HTTP(S), rather than a `file://` URL.
+
+## Rebuild
+
+With Emscripten (`emcc`) installed:
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+```
+
+This compiles `src/smallpt.cpp` into `public/smallpt.js` and `public/smallpt.wasm`. The browser adapter preserves the original ray intersection, materials, and recursive radiance calculation, and replaces file output and the OpenMP loop with incremental RGBA rendering. The UI can restart rendering while the worker yields between batches. Each pass traces four samples per pixel.
+
+## Check without a browser
+
+```sh
+node scripts/check-wasm.cjs
+node --check app.js
+node --check public/worker.js
+```
+
+The module check executes the actual compiled WebAssembly and checks image dimensions, opaque pixels, nonblack output, and changed output when a sphere's color changes.
+
+`public/preview.png` is a 128-sample, 640 × 480 render produced from the same C++ implementation. It is displayed while WebAssembly initializes. Every subsequent frame is rendered on the user's device.
+
+Original project: https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/
+
+Original unmodified source: `src/smallpt-original.cpp`. MIT license: `src/LICENSE.txt`.
